This patch is needed because V8's bigint header uses C++ memory utilities
without directly including the header that declares them.

What it does:
- includes <memory> before using std::unique_ptr and
  std::make_unique_for_overwrite

Why it is needed:
- without it, GCC on Solaris fails the V8 147.4.0 build with unresolved
  std::unique_ptr and std::make_unique_for_overwrite declarations

--- a/v8-147.4.0/v8/src/bigint/bigint.h
+++ b/v8-147.4.0/v8/src/bigint/bigint.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <iostream>
+#include <memory>
 #include <utility>
 
 namespace v8 {
